    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nWhen diff mode is on, scrolling active pane using navigation keys scrolls both panes synchronously. But if scrolling is done using mouse, scrolling active pane scrolls inactive as well, but scrolling inactive DOESN'T scroll active.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nScroll bound pane if binding is set.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-26T14:35:03Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "why is the call in `normal_finish_command` insufficient? https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/123d46436cc3b3df9a339c3e136fd408856a0c28/src/nvim/normal.c#L1057-L1059\r\n\r\nideally this would be handled at a higher layer like that, rather than a mouse-specific patch. ",
